            "text": "Pokémon Winds and Pokémon Waves | Announcement Trailer Skip to main content \n Reduced motion \n Nintendo Switch 2 \n Pokémon Winds and Pokémon Waves | Announcement Trailer\n Description of the video, for accessibility. Different than a caption.\n Description of the video, for accessibility. Different than a caption.\n Pokémon Winds and Pokémon Waves \n A New Stage Is Set for the Pokémon Series\n The Pokémon Winds and Pokémon Waves games, all-new entries in the Pokémon video game series, will be released exclusively on Nintendo Switch 2 in a simultaneous worldwide release in 2027.\n TRAILER \n These new titles feature an open world to explore, with beautiful windswept islands and a vast ocean with glittering waves that ebb and flow. The Pokémon that live in harmony with this region’s lush environment have developed their own unique ecosystems. By visiting these islands, you’re sure to open the door to a brand-new adventure that could only be found here.\n During this adventure, you’ll be able to team up with all kinds of Pokémon to overcome both the difficult road ahead and even the forces of nature that block your path at times.\n Previous gallery item \n Next gallery item \n Active gallery item: 1 of 12.\n A First Look at the Main Characters\n Pokémon Winds \n When Playing\n Pokémon Winds \n Pokémon Waves \n When Playing\n Pokémon Waves \n You, the player, will become the main character in this adventure when you dive into the world of Pokémon Winds and Pokémon Waves . The outfit your character dons will differ between versions. Just what kind of story could be awaiting you?\n Previous gallery item \n Next gallery item \n Active gallery item: 1 of 8.\n Introducing the First Partner Pokémon\n The three Pokémon you can partner up with are Browt, the Bean Chick Pokémon; Pombon, the Puppy Pokémon; and Gecqua, the Water Gecko Pokémon. Choose one to be your partner, and set out on a new adventure together!\n Previous gallery item \n Next gallery item \n Active gallery item: 1 of 5.\n Browt \n Browt\n This Pokémon runs about energetically while photosynthesizing using the leaves on its brow. It’s lively, but it can also be a bit clumsy.\n Category\n Bean Chick Pokémon\n Type\n Grass\n Height\n 1'\n Weight\n 7.7 lbs.\n Ability\n Overgrow\n Pombon \n Pombon\n The area below its throat glows faintly from the heat-generating organ within its lungs. This Pokémon is guileless and friendly.\n Category\n Puppy Pokémon\n Type\n Fire\n Height\n 1'4\" \n Weight\n 14.8 lbs.\n Ability\n Blaze\n Gecqua \n Gecqua\n This Pokémon launches springy balls of water from its tail. Gecqua is very intelligent and maneuvers shrewdly while putting on airs​.\n Category\n Water Gecko Pokémon\n Type\n Water\n Height\n 1'\n Weight\n 9.5 lbs.\n Ability\n Torrent\n Special Pikachu Make Their Debuts\n The latest video featured the appearance of some Pikachu with a brand-new look. Just how could these Pikachu be involved in your adventure? Look forward to future announcements.\n Mr. Windychu \n Mr. Windychu\n Ms. Wavychu \n Ms. Wavychu\n Sign up for our newsletter!\n Subscribe \n Pokémon Winds and Pokémon Waves The Pokemon Company \n Nintendo \n Nintendo Switch Online \n Select your region — United States United States BBB Caru - Kid's Privacy Safe Harbor Rating Pending \n Terms of Use \n Privacy Notice \n Legal Info \n ©Pokémon/Nintendo/Creatures/GAME FREAK\n Pokémon and Nintendo Switch are trademarks of Nintendo.\n Screenshots and footage are from a product in development and not final. Actual gameplay experience may vary.",
